## Implementation plan v2 — executing the feature roadmap (2026-07-16)

The 2026-07-14 protocol plan (Phases 0–4, above) is **largely built** — the detection *engine*
exists. What remains unbuilt is (a) a handful of protocol probes and (b) almost the entire
**product layer**, which the ROI analysis says is where the value is ("capability doesn't sell;
verdicts, consequences, and next steps sell"). This plan sequences the remaining work, grounded in
what is verified present in the tree at HEAD `4adb691` (file presence audited 2026-07-16; presence
≠ verified-complete — MASTERPLAN2/WS7 is the hardening pass over these).

**Foundation already in the engine (do NOT re-plan; build product features ON these):**
Synthesis/verdict (`Conclusion`, `Synthesis/Stage5Presentation`), DNSSEC (`DNSSECVerifier`),
chain-walk (`AuthoritativeVantage`,`CNAMEChainProbe`), NSEC/NSEC3 (`DenialOfExistenceProbe`),
IPv6/DNS64 (`DualStackProbe`), ECS (`ECSProbe`), TTL (`TTLAnomalyProbe`), SVCB
(`SVCBProbe`), resolver-id (`VersionBindProbe`), encrypted transport (`EncryptedTransportProbe`),
leak (`LeakDetector`), latency (`ResolverLatencyProbe`), capture (`DNSCapture`), exfil/tunneling
(`Forensics/ExfilAnalyzer`,`MonitorReportAnalyzer`), mDNS (`LAN/MDNSScanner`), continuous-monitoring
core (`Trust/Sentinel`), signing (`WitnessSigner`,`SignedEvidencePayload`), server passive-DNS
(`passivedns.py`). **Parity note:** the above are enumerated on macOS; every item below ships as a
macOS + Windows twin (`AGENTS.md` parity), server where trust-material is touched.

**Global acceptance discipline (every item):** real run + mutation-proven failing-case test
(Protocol §3/§4); tri-state honesty (missing/timeout/invalid → inconclusive, never silent-good);
GUI-visible copy proposed for approval before shipping (`AGENTS.md:42`).

### Phase A — The "so what" product layer (Tier-1 ROI; engine already supports it, so highest value/effort)

- **A1 — Verdict→Action layer.** Every module + the final `Conclusion` ends in a plain sentence and a
  recommended action, per verdict class. Build: an action-map keyed on hypothesis/verdict →
  {headline, why, do-this}; surface in GUI Conclusions + CLI `showConclusions`. Copy-gated.
  *Bar:* every terminal verdict renders a concrete next step; no dead-end "INCONCLUSIVE".
- **A2 — Plain-language explanation layer** over the Dempster-Shafer output ("we believe X because
  A and B, despite C"). Build: an NL renderer over `Stage5Presentation` reasoning
  (mechanism headline + provenance + within-class). *Bar:* a layperson can restate the verdict cause.
- **A3 — Network report card / letter grade** + top-3 reasons; the shareable screenshot. Build: a
  grading rubric over `Conclusion` confidence/section-statuses; a card view. Depends on A1.
  *Bar:* the same run always yields the same grade; the three reasons are the real top contributors.
- **A4 — Five-minute first-run.** One button → full orchestrated scan → graded result before any
  config. Build: a scan sequencer over `ProbePlan`/`ProbeRunner`/`ProbeBudget`; onboarding flow.
  *Bar:* cold launch to grade with zero configuration, bounded runtime.
- **A5 — Continuous monitoring mode (THE subscription item).** Background re-probe + alerts + state
  persistence. Build ON `Trust/Sentinel` + `MonitorReportAnalyzer`: scheduler, change-detection,
  alert surface, per-network history. *Bar:* a real config drift between two scans raises one alert.
- **A6 — Menu-bar / tray trust indicator.** Glanceable green/amber/red for the current network;
  the psychological anchor for A5. Build: lightweight status item bound to the latest `Conclusion`.
  *Bar:* indicator color always equals the last real verdict; never green on inconclusive.

### Phase B — Trust & shareability (Tier-2 ROI; every share is free acquisition)

